    "title": "Clarify core skill update behavior for local template edits",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "**What**: Remove ambiguity in `kspec skill update` when core templates change locally but package version is unchanged.\n\n**Problem**: `skill update` short-circuits on version match, so same-version template edits are skipped with no clear next action. During local core-skill/template iteration this appears broken, and users only discover later that `skill install-core` was required.\n\n**Scope**:\n1. Update `skill update` behavior in `src/cli/commands/skill-install.ts` so same-version cases are not silently misleading. Acceptable outcomes:\n   - detect template/file drift and still update files, OR\n   - keep version gate but emit explicit guidance (`use kspec skill install-core`) in both normal and `--dry-run` output.\n2. Ensure output clearly distinguishes: version up-to-date vs template content out-of-sync.\n3. Add/adjust tests in `tests/core-skill-update.test.ts` (and `tests/core-skill-install.test.ts` if needed) covering the same-version local-template-change path and expected messaging/behavior.\n\n**Verification**:\n- `npx vitest run tests/core-skill-update.test.ts tests/core-skill-install.test.ts`\n- Manual CLI check on changed-template scenario shows deterministic behavior (update or explicit guidance), including `--dry-run`.\n\n**Done when**:\n1. Same-version template changes are no longer silently skipped without actionable guidance.\n2. Users can reliably tell whether to run `skill update` vs `skill install-core`.\n3. Tests cover the scenario and pass.",
